4. Encryption & sovereignty

On-die key material:

Per-chip master key in secure fuses

Optional user key via host (never leaves chip once loaded)

Encrypted state & logs:

Event ledger, lineage stats, and snapshots stored in on-die SRAM/flash only as ciphertext

Export path always passes through CVE

Controlled plaintext window:

Only high-level metrics (e.g., reward curves, labels, compressed summaries) exposed as plaintext over HIB

Raw internal states never leave unencrypted

Authorship seal:

